    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 4: MARKETING ROI & DIGITAL MARKETING -->
  <div class="blog-section" id="marketing-roi">
    <h2>4. How to Calculate Marketing ROI &amp; Digital Marketing ROI</h2>
    <p>
      Marketing leaders and growth agencies face relentless pressure in 2026 to prove return on digital advertising across Meta, Google Ads, TikTok, and programmatic networks. A common trap is confusing <strong>ROAS (Return on Ad Spend)</strong> with true <strong>Marketing ROI</strong>.
    </p>

    <div class="blog-code">
      <code><span class="comment">// 1. Standard Marketing ROI</span></code>
      <code>Marketing ROI (%) = [ (<span class="hl">Attributable Revenue Growth - Marketing Expense</span>) / <span class="res">Marketing Expense</span> ] × 100</code>
      <code><br><span class="comment">// 2. ROAS Formula (Revenue only, ignores COGS)</span></code>
      <code>ROAS = <span class="hl">Gross Attributable Ad Revenue</span> / <span class="res">Total Ad Spend</span></code>
    </div>

    <h3>ROAS vs. True Marketing ROI: The Critical Distinction</h3>
    <p>
      Suppose a direct-to-consumer lifestyle brand in Los Angeles, California spends $10,000 on Google Search campaigns and generates $40,000 in tracked online sales:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>ROAS:</strong> $40,000 / $10,000 = <strong>4.0x (or 400%)</strong>. On an ad dashboard, this looks stellar.</li>
      <li><strong>Real Cost Breakdown:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Product Manufacturing &amp; COGS (40%): $16,000</li>
          <li>Merchant Processing &amp; 3PL Shipping (10%): $4,000</li>
          <li>Ad Spend: $10,000</li>
          <li>Agency Management Fee: $2,500</li>
          <li><strong>Total Marketing &amp; Delivery Cost:</strong> $32,500</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Net Profit Generated:</strong> $40,000 - $32,500 = $7,500</li>
      <li><strong>True Marketing Net ROI:</strong> ($7,500 / $12,500 total marketing &amp; agency cost) × 100 = <strong>60.0%</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Always evaluate blended customer acquisition cost (CAC) and customer lifetime value (LTV). If your repeat customer rate is high, an initial customer transaction at break-even can compound into an incredible 300%+ ROI over 24 months.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 5: AMAZON FBA & E-COMMERCE -->
  <div class="blog-section" id="amazon-fba-roi">
    <h2>5. How to Calculate ROI on Amazon FBA &amp; E-Commerce</h2>
    <p>
      Selling on Amazon via Fulfillment by Amazon (FBA) requires careful per-unit accounting. Many new sellers in states like Texas and Florida suffer margin squeeze because they fail to incorporate Amazon's tiered fee structures into their inventory investment projections.
    </p>

    <div class="blog-code">
      <code><span class="comment">// Amazon FBA Inventory ROI</span></code>
      <code>Net Profit Per Unit = Retail Price - (Landed COGS + Referral Fee + FBA Fulfillment + PPC Ad Cost)</code>
      <code>FBA ROI (%) = (<span class="hl">Net Profit Per Unit</span> / <span class="res">Landed COGS Per Unit</span>) × 100</code>
    </div>

